    M4.1 patch 1: HoQA m-RC1-1 - explainer entry (expin) without scale overshoot (CSS only)
    
    qa/m41/rc1-5d9efa6-ui.md m-RC1-1: at 375x667 (Upgrades > Farm, scroll
    200, refund card placed 'band', 0.75px clear when settled) the expin
    easing --ease-pop (cubic-bezier(.34,1.56,.64,1)) overshoots scale ~1.0098
    and the card covers the Hens Buy by <=0.27px for ~35 ms.
    
    Fix (CSS only): .tracks-exp expin uses the same curve with y1 1.56 -> 1
    (cubic-bezier(.34,1,.64,1)): same .2s duration, same start (scale .9,
    opacity 0), monotonic to scale 1, no overshoot. --ease-pop is unchanged
    for every other animation. No layout or other visual change.
    
    Proof: rc0 section mrc1 (375x667, scroll 150..260 step 10, the expin
    animation paused and stepped 0..200 ms every 2 ms + settled; the card
    must not intersect any Buy rect clipped to the sheet body; max scale
    <= 1). Before the fix it FAILS (0.257px over Hens at t=114 ms, scale
    1.0098, Chromium); after, worst gap -0.75px (clear) at every sample.

